 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? Totally normal. Think of it as getting dressed up for work. Do you want sit by the waiting staff, or do you want a window? They' worth it. Pick the one you pass on the way to the bathroom. Dress codes mean something to beat you at. Smart casual is the ticket. If you overdo it, everyone will notice. Lots of people don't. You' learn as you go. Order something you like the sound of, and ask for a spoonful of the sauce if you' doubtful. Food developers are gentle people. Probably not. It' worth trying something classic like the beef well done if you' nervous. At least you can always ask for it well done and still feel cool.",
